Description: Rust (candle) inference for Laya's typed-decision engine (CUDA + flash-attn build)
 rlcd answers typed choice/score/noul questions over an arbitrary state
 (text, email, ticket, or JSON) in a single non-autoregressive forward pass
 through a ModernBERT/mmBERT encoder plus a from-scratch decision head. This
 build is linked against CUDA and additionally runs the encoder and decision
 head's attention through a fused flash-attention kernel over an unpadded
 (varlen) sequence layout. Needs an NVIDIA GPU with a host driver compatible
 with the CUDA toolkit version it was built against (see
 https://github.com/apiplant/rlcd-rs/blob/main/packaging/README.md).
 libcuda1 (installed by the NVIDIA driver package) satisfies the runtime
 link; it does not by itself guarantee driver/toolkit compatibility.
